{
  "id": "perky-effect",
  "term": "Perky effect",
  "definition": "The Perky effect is the finding that forming a visual image in the same place as a real visual target can make that target harder to detect. It describes an interaction in which imagery lowers visual sensitivity to the target, suggesting interference between imagined and perceived visual information.",
